{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4550","id":4734633531,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGjTGOw","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4550","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4550.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4550.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4550","number":4550,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29-T05.2: reject malformed metadata UTF-8 and retain PE findings","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.2\nRelated: #1144, #1151\n\n## Finding and correction\n\nThe first 512-case PE campaign at bf85020e6024cdd679a0234d9f050ca7dedddf53 found two uncontrolled native exceptions: seed 1, cases 88 and 463. Invalid UTF-8 in the metadata version field reached the shared fatal decoder before metadata table parsing.\n\nThe public decoder now converts only a TypeError with the exact native code ERR_ENCODING_INVALID_ENCODED_DATA into CilError(\"Invalid UTF-8 text\"). The original error is retained as a nonenumerable cause. Other decoder/argument errors still propagate, and the fuzz classifier remains strict.\n\nThe unchanged CilError class and existing text codecs are extracted into leaf modules. Frozen binary.js shrinks from 41 to 39 lines, with no import cycle or public class-identity change.\n\n## Preserved regression inputs\n\nBoth original hash-named records are promoted byte-for-byte with their input, source identity, finding and effective budgets intact. The normal A29 manifest now replays three production records: these two PE inputs and the earlier Portable PDB compression finding. No passing expectations or budgets were weakened.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Parent public regression: 7 tests, 3 pass and 4 fail.\n- Product correction: 33 focused tests pass.\n- Complete final batch: 34 tests pass; no failures, skips or cancellations.\n- Both complete original PE records replay as controlled PE_VALIDATION rejections, with the original 1,000 ms case and 600,000 ms campaign limits.\n- Final ordinary corpus replay: all 3 inputs rejected in a controlled way, zero findings or unsupported outcomes.\n- Independent source review found no blocking issue.\n- Serial command: `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap tests/a03-utf8-validation.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/binary-targets.test.js tests/conformance/fuzz/retained-corpus.test.js`.\n\nLocal tests ran on Linux with Node 24.19.0. The existing A03 glob discovers the new public API test. Ordinary core does not run Node tests.\n\n### Exact source mapping\n\n| Scope | Tested local commit | Published commit | Identical tree |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Product fix and original replay | 33f754dcac94080842042020719ea6b8a4289e3f | 0a79a303af7fefd66a795ee7aaca6a18e27f6068 | 7e98dec2629b370ff7aaa6a998e9facc2c629be8 |\n| Complete corpus batch | f0362e5e187409daf5766c70157280fe580afeae | c9357cc985ed1dbe2bd2b76f99ef5e3cb81d89a9 | ad548d9c4946465692845da0da15cae373463a2f |\n\n## Changes outside this workstream\n\nThe minimal CIL decoder correction is a prerequisite for A29 PE qualification. All nine live A03 metadata claims and their issue-specific ownership paths were read before editing. Their reserved metadata leaves and table-width test are untouched; no matching hot-file reservation was present.\n\n## Remaining qualification\n\nThe original campaign remains failed: 351,421 ms, 512 cases, two findings. It is not credited toward the required ten-minute post-fix qualification. A separate longer campaign at a clean integrated source is next. Uncoded browser TypeErrors retain their prior behavior; this precise Node fix does not claim browser or all-engine diagnostic normalization. Full #1144/#1151 acceptance and nightly policy remain open.","created_at":"2026-10-04T13:13:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T13:14:33Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T13:14:33Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T13:14:33Z","merge_commit_sha":"8019f2f9b22e26d7c221454f3b751b0b0e0c67df","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12526353617,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU59Ms88AAAAC6qD80Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/labels/size/L","name":"size/L","color":"A14C05","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4550/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4550/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4550/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/statuses/c9357cc985ed1dbe2bd2b76f99ef5e3cb81d89a9","head":{"label":"wieslawsoltes:codex/p4-pe-utf8-validation","ref":"codex/p4-pe-utf8-validation","sha":"c9357cc985ed1dbe